#: templates/security.html:78
msgid "Transport and headers"
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:80
msgid ""
"All traffic is terminated at Cloudflare with HSTS enforced. Plain-HTTP "
"requests are 301'd to HTTPS."
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:81
msgid "Content Security Policy"
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:81
msgid ""
"CSP restricts script sources, blocks inline-eval, and refuses mixed "
"content. Every page sets it explicitly — no opt-outs."
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:82
msgid "Strict referrer + frame ancestors"
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:82
msgid "are set globally to limit leakage and clickjacking."
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:83
msgid "No third-party scripts."
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:83
msgid ""
"No analytics tags, no marketing pixels, no embedded widgets. The only "
"outbound network the page initiates is the XRPL WebSocket cluster "
"(visible in /methodology)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:86
msgid "Admin surface"
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:88
msgid "HMAC-signed admin tokens."
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:88
msgid ""
"Admin routes accept only requests signed with a server-side secret. There"
" is no public admin login form, no password-reset endpoint, and no "
"session cookie that can be replayed."
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:89
msgid "Per-IP rate limits."
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:89
msgid ""
"Every public endpoint that returns data has an explicit rate limit, keyed"
" by Cloudflare's authoritative client IP. No global default — limits are "
"written per-route so health checks and HTML pages stay unthrottled."
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:90
msgid "No write surface from the public web."
msgstr ""

#: templates/security.html:90
msgid ""
"The Flask app reads from Postgres; only the workers running on Charlie's "
"Mac (or the standby Render worker) can write. A leaked DB credential on "
"the Flask side cannot mutate state."
msgstr ""

